tinct paths to responsibility.","material":"Not specified","dimensions":"Not specified in source","bearer":"—","status":"literary","attributes":[],"links":[]},{"id":"narnia.jadis","title":"Jadis / White Witch","universe":"narnia","category":"person","summary":"Ruler who imposes a long winter and turns inhabitants into stone.","source":"The Magician’s Nephew; The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe","matrices":["shadow","mind","spirit"],"function":"Domination, deception, ancient magic.","material":"Not specified","dimensions":"Not specified in source","bearer":"—","status":"literary","attributes":[],"links":[]},{"id":"narnia.caspian","title":"Prince Caspian","universe":"narnia","category":"person","summary":"Telmarine heir who seeks to restore Old Narnia.","source":"Prince Caspian","matrices":["soul","mind","spirit"],"function":"Legitimacy and restoration.","material":"Not specified","dimensions":"Not specified in source","bearer":"—","status":"literary","attributes":[],"links":[]},{"id":"kjv.prodigal-ring","title":"Ring for the returning son","universe":"kjv","category":"ring","summary":"A ring ordered for the returning son in the parable.","source":"Luke 15:22 (KJV)","matrices":["body","soul","spirit"],"function":"Symbol of being welcomed home.","material":"Unspecified","dimensions":"Not specified","bearer":"Returning son","status":"scripture","attributes":[],"links":[]},{"id":"kjv.joseph-ring","title":"Pharaoh’s ring given to Joseph","universe":"kjv","category":"ring","summary":"Pharaoh removes his ring and puts it on Joseph’s hand when investing him with authority.","source":"Genesis 41:42 (KJV)","matrices":["body","soul","mind"],"function":"Signet of delegated authority.","material":"Unspecified","dimensions":"Not specified","bearer":"Joseph","status":"scripture","attributes":[],"links":[]},{"id":"kjv.ahasuerus-ring","title":"King Ahasuerus’s ring","universe":"kjv","category":"ring","summary":"Royal ring transferred as a sign of delegated authority.","source":"Esther 3:10; 8:2 (KJV)","matrices":["body","soul","shadow"],"function":"Official authorization and royal seal.","material":"Unspecified","dimensions":"Not specified","bearer":"Haman → Mordecai","status":"scripture","attributes":[],"links":[]},{"id":"kjv.12-gates","title":"Twelve gates of New Jerusalem","universe":"kjv","category":"gate_vision","summary":"A visionary city with twelve gates, three on each cardinal side, each gate described as a pearl.","source":"Revelation 21:12–13, 21, 25 (KJV)","matrices":["body","mind","spirit"],"function":"Gates of a vision; text says they are not shut by day.","material":"Pearl imagery","dimensions":"No measurements for individual gates","bearer":"New Jerusalem","status":"scripture","attributes":[],"links":[]},{"id":"kjv.gate-e1","title":"East gate 1 of 3","universe":"kjv","category":"gate_vision","summary":"Analytical indexing for one of the three east-facing gates in Revelation’s twelve-gate vision; scripture does not number or individually assign tribal names to these gates.","source":"Revelation 21:12–13, 21 (KJV)","matrices":["body","mind","spirit"],"function":"Visionary city access; positional indexing is editorial.","material":"One pearl per gate (vision)","dimensions":"Not given","bearer":"New Jerusalem","status":"scripture","attributes":[],"links":["kjv.12-gates"]},{"id":"kjv.gate-e2","title":"East gate 2 of 3","universe":"kjv","category":"gate_vision","summary":"Analytical indexing for one of the three east-facing gates in Revelation’s twelve-gate vision; scripture does not number or individually assign tribal names to these gates.","source":"Revelation 21:12–13, 21 (KJV)","matrices":["body","mind","spirit"],"function":"Visionary city access; positional indexing is editorial.","material":"One pearl per gate (vision)","dimensions":"Not given","bearer":"New Jerusalem","status":"scripture","attributes":[],"links":["kjv.12-gates"]},{"id":"kjv.gate-e3","title":"East gate 3 of 3","universe":"kjv","category":"gate_vision","summary