nd":"ring ↔ gate symbolic correspondence","status":"interpretation","explanation":"Assign proposed ring 11 (protection) to a model index for the twelve visionary gates. This is a conceptual mapping, not a scriptural or historical conversion."},{"id":"transform.ring-gate-12","from":"design.ring-12","to":"kjv.gate-w3","kind":"ring ↔ gate symbolic correspondence","status":"interpretation","explanation":"Assign proposed ring 12 (freedom) to a model index for the twelve visionary gates. This is a conceptual mapping, not a scriptural or historical conversion."},{"id":"transform.rings-spirit","from":"lotr.narya","to":"kjv.fruit","kind":"cross-source analogy","status":"interpretation","explanation":"Interpretive comparison: ring kindling courage to qualities of moral character."},{"id":"transform.ring-control","from":"lotr.one","to":"kjv.god-of-world","kind":"cross-source analogy","status":"interpretation","explanation":"Interpretive parallel about domination; not a textual identity or proof of divine theft."},{"id":"transform.arkenstone-innocence","from":"hobbit.arkenstone","to":"kjv.pure-religion","kind":"cross-source analogy","status":"interpretation","explanation":"Symbolic reading of the Arkenstone as innocence; no such identity in Tolkien or scripture."},{"id":"transform.sting-spirit","from":"lotr.sting","to":"kjv.sword-spirit","kind":"cross-source analogy","status":"interpretation","explanation":"Analogical comparison of revealing and discerning; a real story blade remains distinct from a biblical metaphor."},{"id":"transform.glamdring-spirit","from":"lotr.glamdring","to":"kjv.twoedged","kind":"cross-source analogy","status":"interpretation","explanation":"Analogical comparison only; source text does not describe wavelength detection."},{"id":"transform.anduril-restoration","from":"lotr.anduril","to":"kjv.sword-spirit","kind":"cross-source analogy","status":"interpretation","explanation":"Symbolic parallel for restoration and discernment."},{"id":"transform.mithril-armor","from":"lotr.mithril","to":"kjv.armor","kind":"cross-source analogy","status":"interpretation","explanation":"Analogy between physical protection and spiritual readiness; not a nervous-system medical mechanism."},{"id":"transform.wardrobe-gate","from":"narnia.wardrobe","to":"narnia.wardrobe-gate","kind":"functional link","status":"interpretation","explanation":"Functional reinterpretation of furniture as gateway, retaining furniture as source category."},{"id":"transform.narnia-ring-gate","from":"narnia.green","to":"narnia.pool","kind":"functional link","status":"interpretation","explanation":"In-story linkage: a green ring and a world-pool act together during travel, but are not the same physical object."},{"id":"transform.prodigal-restore","from":"kjv.prodigal-ring","to":"design.ring-10","kind":"cross-source analogy","status":"interpretation","explanation":"A biblical ring as a symbol of restored relationship, linked to a proposed wearable ring of service."}],"positions":[{"number":1,"ring_id":"design.ring-01","hand":"Left","part":"Thumb","role":"Choice","gate_id":"kjv.gate-e1"},{"number":2,"ring_id":"design.ring-02","hand":"Left","part":"Index finger","role":"Direction","gate_id":"kjv.gate-e2"},{"number":3,"ring_id":"design.ring-03","hand":"Left","part":"Middle finger","role":"Balance","gate_id":"kjv.gate-e3"},{"number":4,"ring_id":"design.ring-04","hand":"Left","part":"Ring finger","role":"Loyalty","gate_id":"kjv.gate-n1"},{"number":5,"ring_id":"design.ring-05","hand":"Left","part":"Little finger","role":"Care","gate_id":"kjv.gate-n2"},{"number":6,"ring_id":"design.ring-06","hand":"Right","part":"Thumb","role":"Action","gate_id":"kjv.gate-n3"},{"number":7,"ring_id":"design.ring-07","hand":"Right","part":"Index finger","role":"Knowledge","gate_id":"kjv.gate-s1"},{"number":8,"ring_id":"design.ring-08","hand":"Right","part":"Middle finger","role":"Judgment","gate_id":"kjv.gate-s2"},{"number":9,"ring_id":"design.ring-09","hand":"Right","part":"Ring finger","role":"Responsibility","gate_id":"kjv.gate-s3"},{"number":10,"ring_id":"design.ring-10","hand":"Right","part":"Little finger","role":"Service","gate_id":"kjv.gate-w1"},{"number":11,"ring_id":"design.ring-11","hand":"Left arm","part":"Bracelet","role":"Protection","gate_id":"kjv.gate-w2"},{"number":12,"ring_id":"design.ring-12","hand":"Right arm","part":"Bracelet","role":"Freedom","gate_id":"kjv.gate-w3"}],"events":[{"id":"evt.01","universe":"lotr","date":"Second Age","name":"Forging of the Rings","description":"The Rings of Power and the One Ring establish the historical background for the later quest."},{"id":"evt.02","universe":"hobbit","date":"Third Age 2941","name":"The Quest for Erebor","description":"Bilbo acquires the One Ring; the dragon Smaug falls; Erebor is reclaimed."},{"id":"evt.03","universe":"lotr","date":"Third Age 3018–3019","name":"War of the Ring","description":"The fellowship’s journey ends with the Ring’s destruction."},{"id":"evt.04","universe":"narnia","date":"Narnian creation","name":"The Magician’s Nephew","description":"The Wood, Magic Rings, creation of Narnia, and Wardrobe’s origin."},{"id":"evt.05","universe":"narnia","date":"Later Narnian era","name":"The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe","description":"Pevensies, gifts, Stone Table, and fall of Jadis."},{"id":"evt.06","universe":"narnia","date":"Centuries later in Narnia","name":"Prince Caspian","description":"Caspian uses the horn and helps restore Old Narnia."},{"id":"evt.07","universe":"kjv","date":"Textual reference","name":"Twelve gates in Revelation","description":"A city with three gates to each cardinal direction, not prescribed finger rings."},{"id":"evt.08","universe":"design","date":"Interpretive model","name":"Twelve-ring restoration proposal","description":"Ten finger/thumb positions and two arm bracelets; explicitly symbolic."}],"scripture":[{"ref":"Genesis 41:42","topic":"Joseph receives Pharaoh’s ring","type":"explicit physical ring","objects":["kjv.joseph-ring"]},{"ref":"Esther 3:10; 8:2","topic":"King’s ring and delegated authority","type":"explicit physical ring","objects":["kjv.ahasuerus-ring"]},{"ref":"Luke 15:22","topic":"Ring for the returning son","type":"explicit physical ring","objects":["kjv.prodigal-ring"]},{"ref":"Revelation 21:12–13, 21, 25","topic":"Twelve gates; three each direction; one pearl each; not shut by day","type":"visionary gates","objects":["kjv.12-gates"]},{"ref":"Exodus 27:16–18","topic":"Court gate hanging and measurements","type":"literal gate","objects":["kjv.tabernacle-gate"]},{"ref":"Acts 12:10","topic":"Iron city gate","type":"literal gate","objects":["kjv.iron-gate"]},{"ref":"Matthew 7:13–14","topic":"Strait and wide gates","type":"figurative gate","objects":["kjv.narrow-gate"]},{"ref":"Psalm 24:7–10","topic":"Everlasting gates addressed poetically","type":"figurative gate","objects":["kjv.everlasting-gates"]},{"ref":"Exodus 25:10–40","topic":"Ark, mercy seat, table, and lampstand","type":"physical furniture","objects":["kjv.ark","kjv.mercy-seat","kjv.table","kjv.candlestick"]},{"ref":"Exodus 27:1–8","topic":"Brazen altar","type":"physical furniture","objects":["kjv.altar"]},{"ref":"Genesis 3:24","topic":"Flaming sword guarding the way","type":"visionary / narrative weapon","objects":["kjv.flame-sword"]},{"ref":"Ephesians 6:13–17","topic":"Armor and sword of the Spirit","type":"spiritual metaphor","objects":["kjv.armor","kjv.sword-spirit"]},{"ref":"Hebrews 4:12","topic":"Twoedged sword comparison","type":"spiritual metaphor","objects":["kjv.twoedged"]},{"ref":"Romans 13:4","topic":"Sword of governing authority","type":"legal imagery","objects":["kjv.romans-sword"]},{"ref":"Galatians 5:22–23","topic":"Fruit of the Spirit","type":"moral text","objects":["kjv.fruit"]},{"ref":"James 1:27","topic":"Pure religion: care for vulnerable people","type":"moral text","objects":["kjv.pure-religion"]},{"ref":"Luke 10:25–37","topic":"Good Samaritan parable","type":"moral narrative","objects":["kjv.good-samaritan"]},{"ref":"Job 5:13","topic":"Craftiness reversed in Eliphaz’s speech","type":"speech / thematic analogy","objects":["kjv.job"]},{"ref":"Psalm 50:12","topic":"Claim of divine ownership","type":"psalm","objects":["kjv.psalm-ownership"]},{"ref":"2 Corinthians 4:4","topic":"God of this world wording","type":"epistle","objects":["kjv.god-of-world"]}],"glossary":[{"language":"English","ring":"ring","gate":"gate","note":"English labels for the central model."},{"language":"Hebrew","ring":"טַבַּעַת — tabbaʿat","gate":"שַׁעַר — shaʿar","note":"Transliterations approximate; semantic range varies by context."},{"language":"Greek","ring":"δακτύλιος — daktylios","gate":"πύλη — pylē","note":"Gate words include pylē and pylōn, depending on context."},{"language":"Latin","ring":"anulus","gate":"porta","note":"Classical forms; other synonyms also exist."},{"language":"Arabic","ring":"خاتم — khātam","gate":"باب — bāb","note":"Khātam can mean seal or signet ring."}]};
</script>
